  clock: 6  # c244
  nonce: c244  # c244
  message: "Tag added 2026-05-07 per validation-modality-mapping conversation (extension to consideration-leftovers). The Wave 4 Cluster F dst-kind leakage fold (commit 689744022) shipped the producer migration without the awaits_bakeoff_validation tag. This entry retroactively establishes the queue claim.\n\nValidation modality:\n\nDEEP (primary): cohort comparing pre-Wave-4 to post-Wave-6 behavior maps. Expected metric movements: (1) component_ref values fold from kind='component_ref' to kind='reference' with the dst-side discrimination (dst.kind=='component') carrying the framework-component identification per audit-findings 0011; (2) consumer query patterns at component-resolution surfaces (route_handler, framework-pattern matchers) — the dual representation (Symbol-side reference + Edge-side relationship) preserves component-resolution semantics; (3) edge graph reachability and slice membership for component declarations vs component usages.\n\nUAT (supplementary, per-framework spot-checks): Vue SFC monorepo (component_ref imports across .vue files); Svelte 4/5 repo (component imports); Astro repo (.astro frontmatter component_ref imports — note this is a separate concern from astro.py's separate import-edge work in WI-kunag); React/JSX repo with hand-rolled component-import-tracking. The fold is structural — UAT spot-checks confirm consumer behavior is preserved; aggregate metric movement may be small if the consumer query was already through the dst.kind discrimination.\n\nCoverage overlap with WI-gajob (Cluster B FOLDs, particularly component_file→file): the post-fold consumer at route_handler.is_component reads kind='file' + meta['module_system'] OR meta['component_framework']. WI-mihiz validates the component-ref Symbol's resolution-path side; WI-gajob validates the component-file Symbol's file-shape side. Both folds together are exercised by the same Vue monorepo UAT target."  # c244
